%I A400196 #17 Oct 09 2026 10:57:10
%S A400196 0,1,-1,-2,2,3,4,5,-4,-3,-5,-6,-7,-8,8,6,7,9,10,11,12,13,-12,-10,-9,
%T A400196 -11,-13,-14,-15,-16,-17,-18,18,14,15,16,17,19,20,21,22,23,24,25,-24,
%U A400196 -20,-19,-21,-22,-23,-25,-26,-27,-28,-29,-30,-31,-32,32,28,26,27,29,30,31
%N A400196 The Heraclitus transform of the squares and 2: a(0) = 0; thereafter a(n) is the least integer (in absolute value) not yet in the sequence such that the absolute difference between a(n-1) and a(n) is either a square or 2; in case of a tie, preference is given to the positive value.
%C A400196 This sequence contains every positive and negative integer. The author has a proof which is to be posted on the SeqFan mailing list.
%C A400196 From _Geoffrey Caveney_, Oct 03 2026: (Start)
%C A400196 The proof shows by induction that for every nonnegative integer k, the terms a(0), ..., a((2k)^2) comprise all the integers m such that |m| <= (2k)^2 / 2, and that a((2k)^2 + 1) = (2k)^2 / 2 + 1. Each section of the sequence from the term a((2k)^2 + 1) to the term a((2(k+1))^2) contains four blocks:
%C A400196 Block A: positive integers from (2k)^2 / 2 + 1 in order of increasing absolute value up to ((2k+1)^2 + 1) / 2.
%C A400196 Block B: the negative integer -[((2k+1)^2 - 1) / 2], various steps of decreasing absolute value to -[(2k)^2 / 2 + 1], then steps of increasing absolute value in differences of 1 or 2 to -[((2k+1)^2 + 1) / 2].
%C A400196 Block C: negative integers from -[((2k+1)^2 + 3) / 2] in order of increasing absolute value up to -[(2k+2)^2 / 2].
%C A400196 Block D: the positive integer (2k+2)^2 / 2, various steps of decreasing absolute value to ((2k+1)^2 + 3) / 2, then steps of increasing absolute value in differences of 1 or 2 to (2k+2)^2 / 2 - 1. (End)
%H A400196 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400196/b400196.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%e A400196 The initial terms are:
%e A400196   n   a(n)  |a(n)-a(n-1)|
%e A400196   --  ----  -------------
%e A400196    0     0  N/A
%e A400196    1     1  1^2
%e A400196    2    -1  2
%e A400196    3    -2  1^2
%e A400196    4     2  2^2
%e A400196    5     3  1^2
%e A400196    6     4  1^2
%e A400196    7     5  1^2
%e A400196    8    -4  3^2
%e A400196    9    -3  1^2
%e A400196   10    -5  2
%e A400196   11    -6  1^2
%e A400196   12    -7  1^2
%e A400196   13    -8  1^2
%e A400196   14     8  4^2
%t A400196 A400196list[nmax_] := Module[{s, a, u = 1}, s[_] := False; NestList[(While[s[u] && s[-u], u++]; a = u; While[s[a] || (# != 2 && !IntegerQ[Sqrt[#]] & [Abs[# - a]]), a = Boole[a < 0] - a]; s[a] = True; a) &, 0, nmax]];
%t A400196 A400196list[100] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 09 2026 *)
%Y A400196 Cf. A377091, A400197, A000290, A383442.
